{
 "title": "When Demand Rises: Effect on Price",
 "lang": "en",
 "steps": [
  {
   "title": "Market Axes",
   "say": "Let's draw a standard supply and demand graph with Price on the vertical axis and Quantity on the horizontal axis.",
   "ops": [
    {
     "op": "write",
     "id": "main_title",
     "x": 800,
     "y": 50,
     "text": "What Happens When Demand Rises?",
     "size": 56,
     "anchor": "middle",
     "underline": true
    },
    {
     "op": "line",
     "id": "y_axis",
     "x1": 220,
     "y1": 750,
     "x2": 220,
     "y2": 150,
     "arrow": true,
     "width": 5
    },
    {
     "op": "line",
     "id": "x_axis",
     "x1": 220,
     "y1": 750,
     "x2": 950,
     "y2": 750,
     "arrow": true,
     "width": 5
    },
    {
     "op": "write",
     "id": "y_label",
     "x": 70,
     "y": 150,
     "text": "Price (P)",
     "size": 32
    },
    {
     "op": "write",
     "id": "x_label",
     "x": 800,
     "y": 780,
     "text": "Quantity (Q)",
     "size": 32
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "title": "Initial Equilibrium",
   "say": "First, we have our upward-sloping Supply curve S, and downward-sloping Demand curve D1, meeting at equilibrium E1.",
   "ops": [
    {
     "op": "line",
     "id": "s_curve",
     "x1": 300,
     "y1": 650,
     "x2": 800,
     "y2": 200,
     "color": "blue",
     "width": 5
    },
    {
     "op": "write",
     "id": "s_label",
     "x": 815,
     "y": 180,
     "text": "S",
     "size": 36,
     "color": "blue"
    },
    {
     "op": "line",
     "id": "d1_curve",
     "x1": 300,
     "y1": 300,
     "x2": 750,
     "y2": 700,
     "color": "green",
     "width": 5
    },
    {
     "op": "write",
     "id": "d1_label",
     "x": 765,
     "y": 685,
     "text": "D1",
     "size": 36,
     "color": "green"
    },
    {
     "op": "ellipse",
     "id": "e1_dot",
     "cx": 500,
     "cy": 473,
     "rx": 8,
     "ry": 8,
     "color": "ink",
     "fill": "ink"
    },
    {
     "op": "write",
     "id": "e1_label",
     "x": 450,
     "y": 430,
     "text": "E1",
     "size": 32
    },
    {
     "op": "line",
     "id": "p1_dash",
     "x1": 220,
     "y1": 473,
     "x2": 500,
     "y2": 473,
     "color": "gray",
     "dash": true,
     "width": 3
    },
    {
     "op": "write",
     "id": "p1_label",
     "x": 165,
     "y": 455,
     "text": "P1",
     "size": 32
    },
    {
     "op": "line",
     "id": "q1_dash",
     "x1": 500,
     "y1": 473,
     "x2": 500,
     "y2": 750,
     "color": "gray",
     "dash": true,
     "width": 3
    },
    {
     "op": "write",
     "id": "q1_label",
     "x": 485,
     "y": 765,
     "text": "Q1",
     "size": 32
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "title": "Demand Shifts Right",
   "say": "When demand rises, consumers want more at every price, shifting the demand curve to the right from D1 to D2.",
   "ops": [
    {
     "op": "line",
     "id": "d2_curve",
     "x1": 450,
     "y1": 250,
     "x2": 900,
     "y2": 650,
     "color": "red",
     "width": 5
    },
    {
     "op": "write",
     "id": "d2_label",
     "x": 915,
     "y": 635,
     "text": "D2",
     "size": 36,
     "color": "red"
    },
    {
     "op": "line",
     "id": "shift_arrow",
     "x1": 390,
     "y1": 370,
     "x2": 510,
     "y2": 320,
     "color": "red",
     "arrow": true,
     "width": 4
    },
    {
     "op": "write",
     "id": "note1",
     "x": 1020,
     "y": 220,
     "text": "1. Demand rises (D1 -> D2)",
     "size": 36,
     "color": "red"
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "title": "Temporary Shortage at P1",
   "say": "At the old price P1, consumers now demand Q_d, which is much more than suppliers make at Q1. This creates a shortage.",
   "ops": [
    {
     "op": "line",
     "id": "shortage_ext",
     "x1": 500,
     "y1": 473,
     "x2": 700,
     "y2": 473,
     "color": "red",
     "dash": true,
     "width": 3
    },
    {
     "op": "ellipse",
     "id": "qd_dot",
     "cx": 700,
     "cy": 473,
     "rx": 7,
     "ry": 7,
     "color": "red",
     "fill": "red"
    },
    {
     "op": "line",
     "id": "qd_dash",
     "x1": 700,
     "y1": 473,
     "x2": 700,
     "y2": 750,
     "color": "gray",
     "dash": true,
     "width": 3
    },
    {
     "op": "write",
     "id": "qd_label",
     "x": 680,
     "y": 765,
     "text": "Qd",
     "size": 32,
     "color": "red"
    },
    {
     "op": "line",
     "id": "shortage_brace",
     "x1": 515,
     "y1": 515,
     "x2": 685,
     "y2": 515,
     "color": "red",
     "arrow": "both",
     "width": 4
    },
    {
     "op": "write",
     "id": "shortage_label",
     "x": 600,
     "y": 530,
     "text": "Shortage",
     "size": 30,
     "color": "red",
     "anchor": "middle"
    },
    {
     "op": "write",
     "id": "note2",
     "x": 1020,
     "y": 300,
     "text": "2. Shortage at P1 (Qd > Q1)",
     "size": 36,
     "color": "ink"
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "title": "Price Rises to New Equilibrium",
   "say": "Buyers compete for limited goods, pushing the price up to P2 until the market reaches a new equilibrium E2.",
   "ops": [
    {
     "op": "erase",
     "ids": [
      "shortage_ext",
      "qd_dot",
      "qd_dash",
      "qd_label",
      "shortage_brace",
      "shortage_label"
     ]
    },
    {
     "op": "ellipse",
     "id": "e2_dot",
     "cx": 603,
     "cy": 377,
     "rx": 8,
     "ry": 8,
     "color": "red",
     "fill": "red"
    },
    {
     "op": "write",
     "id": "e2_label",
     "x": 585,
     "y": 325,
     "text": "E2",
     "size": 32,
     "color": "red"
    },
    {
     "op": "line",
     "id": "p2_dash",
     "x1": 220,
     "y1": 377,
     "x2": 603,
     "y2": 377,
     "color": "red",
     "dash": true,
     "width": 3
    },
    {
     "op": "write",
     "id": "p2_label",
     "x": 165,
     "y": 360,
     "text": "P2",
     "size": 32,
     "color": "red"
    },
    {
     "op": "line",
     "id": "q2_dash",
     "x1": 603,
     "y1": 377,
     "x2": 603,
     "y2": 750,
     "color": "red",
     "dash": true,
     "width": 3
    },
    {
     "op": "write",
     "id": "q2_label",
     "x": 588,
     "y": 765,
     "text": "Q2",
     "size": 32,
     "color": "red"
    },
    {
     "op": "line",
     "id": "p_up_arrow",
     "x1": 140,
     "y1": 455,
     "x2": 140,
     "y2": 385,
     "color": "red",
     "arrow": true,
     "width": 5
    },
    {
     "op": "line",
     "id": "q_up_arrow",
     "x1": 535,
     "y1": 785,
     "x2": 575,
     "y2": 785,
     "color": "red",
     "arrow": true,
     "width": 5
    },
    {
     "op": "write",
     "id": "note3",
     "x": 1020,
     "y": 380,
     "text": "3. Buyers bid up the price",
     "size": 36,
     "color": "ink"
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "title": "Conclusion",
   "say": "In conclusion, when demand rises while supply remains constant, both the equilibrium price and quantity increase!",
   "ops": [
    {
     "op": "rect",
     "id": "sum_box",
     "x": 1000,
     "y": 480,
     "w": 530,
     "h": 220,
     "color": "blue",
     "fill": "blue",
     "width": 4
    },
    {
     "op": "write",
     "id": "sum_title",
     "x": 1265,
     "y": 505,
     "text": "Conclusion:",
     "size": 40,
     "color": "blue",
     "anchor": "middle",
     "underline": true
    },
    {
     "op": "write",
     "id": "sum_p",
     "x": 1040,
     "y": 570,
     "text": "• Equilibrium Price RISES (P1 -> P2)",
     "size": 32,
     "color": "red"
    },
    {
     "op": "write",
     "id": "sum_q",
     "x": 1040,
     "y": 630,
     "text": "• Equilibrium Quantity RISES (Q1 -> Q2)",
     "size": 32,
     "color": "ink"
    }
   ]
  }
 ]
}